/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  cavett01_recycle_train  --  the field's oldest recycle benchmark, on its
                              PRIMARY specification.

  SOURCES.  R. H. Cavett, "Application of Numerical Methods to the
  Convergence of Simulated Processes Involving Recycle Loops", Proc. API
  43 (1963) 57.  Specification and published solutions: E. M. Rosen &
  A. C. Pauls, Comput. Chem. Eng. 1 (1977) 11 (FLOWTRAN); E. M. Rosen,
  "VMGSim: Revisiting the Cavett Problem", CACHE News, Fall 2005 (feed
  table, stage conditions, and both solutions side by side); also Seader &
  Henley, Separation Process Principles (1998), Exercise 10.35.

  THE SPEC, from Rosen (2005), Fig. 3:
      stage        T          P
      FL1        100 F     800 psia     (310.928 K, 55.1581 bar)
      FL2        120 F     270 psia     (322.039 K, 18.6159 bar)
      FL3         96 F      49 psia     (308.706 K,  3.3784 bar)
      FL4         85 F      13 psia     (302.594 K,  0.8963 bar)
      feed       120 F     270 psia,  16 components, total 27340.6
  (original flows lbmol/hr; declared in 0/feed as kmol/h with the same
  numerals -- a uniform scale, stated there.)  The flowsheet is a
  four-stage NEAR-ISOTHERMAL distillation (Gunther, US 3,575,077): FL1 the
  partial condenser, FL4 the partial reboiler, feed on stage 2; products
  P1 (FL1 vapour) and P2 (FL4 liquid).

  WHAT THE RUN SHOWS, measured on this spec:

    * Newton on the two torn mixer outlets: 7 iterations to |r| = 4e-9.
      Wegstein per-component acceleration STALLS: 300 iterations
      limit-cycling at |dtear| ~ 1.4e-2, exit 1, no converged/ written --
      the contract behaving exactly as ratified.  On the primary
      conditions the 1963 pathology is not slow, it is DEFEATING: propane
      circulates at 35716 kmol/h in mixed2 against 2291 fed (a 15.6x loop
      buildup), and the accelerator chases a moving inventory.  (Swap
      `recycleSolver` in system/solverDict to see both.)

    * The K-MODEL SENSITIVITY, quantified against the published
      solutions.  This case declares SRK (k_ij = 0); Rosen's 2005 table
      solves the same spec with an advanced Peng-Robinson package, beside
      the 1977 FLOWTRAN values.  Our lights agree to <1 % (N2 358.2
      exact, CH4 2995.4 vs 2995.3, ethane in P1 2383.8 vs 2378.3) and the
      loop intermediates carry the model difference (isoButane in P1:
      153.9 here, 197.7 APR, 198.2 FLOWTRAN) -- stream values were never
      the portable part of this benchmark, and here is the measurement of
      exactly how un-portable, component by component.

    * A published table is not scripture: Rosen points out the 1977
      FLOWTRAN ethane row is internally inconsistent (2883.2 in P1 where
      the component balance wants ~2383.2 -- a transcription slip, 502
      mol/h of imbalance in print for 28 years).  Our SRK P1 ethane lands
      at 2383.8.  Check the source's own balance before trusting it: this
      case's P1+P2 closes against the feed to 0.05 kmol/h worst-component
      (~1e-5 relative, the declared tear tolerance).

  HISTORY.  The first commit of this case ran a topology reconstructed
  from paraphrases (primary blocked from the hosted session) and said so
  in this header.  The primary arrived and showed 2 of 11 edges wrong
  (feed entered the wrong mixer; V4 recycled one stage too high) plus
  soft conditions where the real ones are sharp.  Everything above is
  from the source; the lesson about citing from memory is kept in the
  flowsheetDict header.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoSolve;
description   "Cavett (1963) four-flash recycle benchmark on the primary Rosen-Pauls spec: 2 tears, Newton 7 it (Wegstein defeated), SRK vs published APR/FLOWTRAN products";

verbosity     3;
